WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.560
Yakitate!! 9!

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.940
The sixth match.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.110
The person who now faced the Pantasia team was...

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.820
Miki Norihei of Gohan Desuyo fame!

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.160
I-Isn’t that guy from Momoya?

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:13.820
Yeah.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.830
I-I can’t believe it.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.330
To think that they brought in someone this big...

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.750
I wonder if they’re all right with all the rights issues...

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.830
I-I wouldn’t know...

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.170
And the place for the showdown is...

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.920
the most famous producer of seaweed,
the item that Norihei specializes in...

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.340
Uppurui.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.590
I-It’s over!

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.800
Well, instead of small talk,
would you try eating this?

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.520
This is Gohan Desuyo, which
I’ve changed to better suit bread.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.690
You just spread it on toast like this.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.310
Come, try it?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.020
Th-Thank you.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.950
Well, here I go.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.820
Th-This is...!

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.160
How is it?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.580
Isn’t it quite good?

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:58.790
This is...!

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.450
The program’s title has changed!

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:04.040
The logo’s been changed to “It’s Yakitate!! Japan!”

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.960
I didn’t notice!

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.880
Yeah.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.340
This is truly the most amazing
reaction ever!

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.840
It’s causing an unbelievable
amount of trouble to everyone!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.090
But, I’m sure that this is...

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.430
the true strength of that man.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.480
In order to stand up to this fearsome opponent,
Kazuma came up with a secret plan.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.060
That is...

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.860
We’re going to boil it.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.560
We’re going to boil it in this Pepmi-Cola!

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.810
Pepmi

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:30.990
I see!

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.030
Brewing it in cola, huh?

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.030
It refers to a technique where things like various meats or marine plants like kelp

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.410
can be softened by brewing them in cola
because of the carbon dioxide present in it.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.910
Seaweed is a marine plant like kelp, after all...

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.540
So, it should work well with seaweed as well.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.540
Come, try some.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.250
Why do I have to do this?!

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.210
Th-This is...!

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.180
Help me!

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.100
That’s...!

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.520
Help me!

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.490
It’s Kawachi-san!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.110
No, it’s Pepmiman!

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:18.870
In addition to that...!

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.870
All we need to do is make the
dough fluffy like freshly made rice.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.870
What are you, an idiot?!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.120
Listen up, Azuma.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.210
To make a fluffy bread like freshly made rice
is considered to be a dream for all bakers.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:31.880
Fluffy

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.930
Even if you’re a genius, something
like that can’t possibly be easy...

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:36.880
It’s possible.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.720
What was that?!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.350
Very well then.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:43.640
We will now start the sixth match
of Yakitate!! 9 here in Uppurui.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.890
Begin!

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:51.520
And now, the showdown begins with guns cocked.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.360
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.280
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.530
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:05.000
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:10.080
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.800
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:24.600
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:30.770
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:45.870
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:54.460
probably helped me notice that

00:03:54.460 --> 00:04:00.340
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:09.230
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:14.600
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:21.740
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:27.530
that white sky with my colors.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:34.540
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.920
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.270
A traditional taste!!

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.990
The heart that thinks of Japan is just one!

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.440
Good luck, Azuma!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.790
After all, this is the all-important match with five panels,

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.330
including the one from the match we drew on, at stake.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.070
So, I’m getting all fired up
over the cheering.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.070
Kawachi-san...

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.660
Looks like, from the very beginning, you’re no longer even allowed into the kitchen.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.080
Yeah, he’s so pitiful that I don’t even
feel like making fun of him anymore.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.330
Azuma! Hang in there!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.710
K... Kawachi-san...

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.260
What is that?

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.300
It almost looks like
he’s foaming detergent.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.140
Tsukino, you know...

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.510
There’s no way that I could
possibly know now, is there?

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.970
Figure it out already.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:34.980
Sorry about that.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.440
That’s butter.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:38.690
Butter?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.650
The process of whipping butter before
you add it to the dough is called creaming.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.660
If you do that, the dough becomes fluffy.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.410
Just as you’d expect of Azuma...

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.910
To think that he knew of such a technique...

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.620
With this, even if our opponent
does better at making the seaweed,

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.000
we should be able to fight back with the bread.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:55.700
No!

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.160
It won’t be that easy.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.120
Look carefully.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.460
Miki-san is using the same strategy as Azuma.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.670
What was that?!

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:10.680
It’s true that in the past,
I never held much interest in bread.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.100
But, Azuma Kazuma-kun...

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:18.810
Once I heard of your existence, I came to want
to fight a serious battle over bread with you.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.500
Even if our specialties are different,

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.900
it is natural for a cook to want to fight against a top-notch man.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.490
I’m serious as well.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.200
I won’t let you get ahead of
me on the bread that easily!

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.870
H-How can this be...?

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.000
If he has the same strategy as us for the bread,

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.210
it’s not possible for us to win against somebody
who’s obviously better at preparing the seaweed!

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:43.250
This is almost like our defeat has
been decided on from the very beginning.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.750
What can we do?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.750
Well, wait.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.430
It’s true that right now,
Azuma’s bread has no hope of winning.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.890
But that is only if he has no
other strategies up his sleeve.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.180
As yet, all that Azuma has done is whip the butter.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.890
He’s not added it to the bread.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:04.190
He might have another strategy
before he starts the first fermentation.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.690
N-Now that you say it...

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:09.650
All we need to do is make the
dough fluffy like freshly made rice.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.820
He said that with complete confidence.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.660
Say, more importantly...

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.410
Have you ever made spring rolls, Kanmuri?

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.250
He’d also mentioned something like that.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:24.710
Creamed butter alone cannot have anything
to do with spring rolls and freshly made rice.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.340
We’re talking about Azuma here.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.210
I’m sure he has another trick up his sleeve.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.720
Some time later

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.470
All right.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.760
I guess this should do it with the dough.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.350
First fermentation. Time for the first fermentation.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.850
Um... If my eyes aren’t deceiving me...

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:45.480
I believe he’s not done any special tricks after that.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.440
Me too.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.610
There weren’t any.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.400
But, he may be planning on doing something now.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.200
What are you, an idiot?!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.870
You’re no amateur yourself, so you must know!

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.870
When making bread, once you’re
done with kneading it, all that’s left is...

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:57.870
The first fermentation.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.870
Letting out the gas.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.870
The second fermentation.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:00.910
And baking.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.620
There can be no sequence other than this!

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:07.540
If you do anything to dough that’s been
fermented once besides letting out the gas,

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.630
the gluten and stuff that was formed
while kneading it would all be broken down.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.130
Well, that’s true I guess...

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.560
Well, looks like it’s about time.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.480
All right!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.810
Wh-What’s he doing?

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.860
That’s not letting out the gas.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.360
No matter how you look at it, he seems
to be kneading the fermented dough again.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.110
Even if our loss is decided, you
can’t make a throwaway bread.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:33.280
I’ll...

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.780
Stop, Kawachi!
I’ll...

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.830
He’s not throwing away the match.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.500
What he’s doing right now is a legendary technique called the remix technique.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.250
What was that?!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.670
The remix technique.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.250
Also known as the re-kneading technique.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:52.670
Re-kneading the dough like that
allows for the formation of firmer gluten.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.260
This will give you a high-quality
dough with a fluffy consistency.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:59.070
It’s true that if you re-knead the dough after the first fermentation,

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.560
the gluten will be broken down.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:05.060
But, even if broken down, it’s not
like the gluten is going to disappear.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.770
It is still within the dough.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.110
I see!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:12.150
So if you knead it again,
the old gluten is rejoined,

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.490
and you get to make new gluten as well.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.820
That’s right.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.870
Gluten is rather like the pillars that hold up the bread.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.700
A greater number of pillars allows
for more air to be trapped inside.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.330
This makes it fluffy.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.700
I-I see!

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:26.790
Well, it’s not surprising that you didn’t know about this.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.540
In addition to it being a real pain to do,
if you mess up, the gluten gets crushed.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.460
That would leave you with
just a hard bread.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.970
This technique is not used at bakeries anymore.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.930
Azuma is really amazing.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.970
If I were in the kitchen...

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.430
What are you doing, you moron?!

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:46.480
Don’t get in my way!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:50.980
Looks like he was right in not letting
me into the kitchen from the very start.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.190
Kanmuri!

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:55.860
How are the raw spring rolls and the
cola-brewed Uppurui seaweed looking?

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.820
All done.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.240
All right!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.820
Let’s put them into the dough then.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.620
All right, looks like things are going well.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.370
Yeah.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.200
Uppurui

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:07.710
When I heard that the match was to be held in
Uppurui, where the specialty product is seaweed...

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.380
I’d given up for a while.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.210
But, he’s come up with the great
strategies of cola-brewed seaweed,

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.210
the creaming technique and the remix technique.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:17.380
With this, we might be able to win!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.890
All right, it’s done!

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:25.140
Mister Kuroyanagi, sample it please.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:27.430
Let’s see it then.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.980
This is...!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.820
As expected of Uppurui seaweed!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.400
Even though it’s stuffed in the bread,
an elegant aroma comes wafting through.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:36.940
Very well then.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.670
K... Kuro-yan...?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.180
15 minutes later

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.600
30 minutes later

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:14.650
Wh... Where in the world could Kuro-yan have gone?

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:18.610
It’s been... almost 30 minutes already.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.240
We’ve never had an incident

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.240
where he’s disappeared for a long
period of time without having a reaction.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.620
That’s not right, Kawachi.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.490
M-Manager!

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:28.830
Why am I on your shoulders again?!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.710
The reaction has already begun.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.000
What was that?!

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.540
Listen up, guys.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:37.000
In this world, it is important to
always look at things from a different angle.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.590
Kawachi, what do you see from there?

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.670
Wh-What do you mean, “what”?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.100
What’s wrong?

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.100
Wh-What’s this?

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.600
There seem to be a lot of
people introducing themselves...

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.060
Hello, I’m Shimada.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:54.230
I’m Shimaki.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:55.230
I’m Shimochiki.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.230
Wh-What does this mean?!

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.230
I’m Shimano.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.230
I’m Shimai.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.240
I’m Shimakawa.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:01.450
No way...

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.240
All of them have a “Shima” in their name.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.700
A-And...

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.830
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6...

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:07.830
I’m Shimaguchi.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.330
I’m Shimao.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.080
I’m Shimatani.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:11.250
I’m Shimabukuro.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:12.580
I’m Shimakura.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.170
8, 9,10,11...

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.170
I’m Shimato.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.500
I’m Shimamura.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:19.630
I’m Shimamoto!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:20.970
There’s 14 of them!

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:23.130
There’s 14 with Shima attached to their names!

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.050
Sorry for the wait.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.510
Kuro-yan...

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.220
Where were you all this time?

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:31.230
The town hall.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.800
At the town hall I carried out the procedures to marry this lady, Ms. Shima,

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.810
and be adopted into her family.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.020
I’m Shima.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.820
Pleased to meet you.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.900
M-Marriage and adoption?!

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.900
Y-You got married?!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.820
That’s right.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:45.950
My name is Shima Ryou as of today.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.410
Sh-Shima...?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:49.450
Get it now, Kawachi?!

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.120
The 14 people with Shima in their
names, plus Shima Ryou and wife.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.290
Giving you 16 people in all with Shima in their names!

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.380
16 islands!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.790
In other words... It’s Uppurui!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.750
What was that?!

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.960
He got married for the sake of his reaction?!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.720
Make me happy, ’kay Mister?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:09.180
Well, since we’ve just met and I don’t even
know your name, I can’t make any guarantees.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.220
However, I shall do my best.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.560
Well then, we have our honeymoon now, so excuse us.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.110
Ummm...

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.980
Well, I guess...

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:23.900
I should congratulate you,
Kuro-yan... I mean Shima-yan...

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.030
I wish you eternal happiness.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:31.540
So, what are we going to do now without the judge?!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.950
Don’t ask me.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:44.260
Kuro-yan got married
and is now Shima-yan.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.260
And he’s gone off on his honeymoon...

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:51.390
To think he just had his reaction and ran off without
any explanations or completing the next judgment...

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.140
No!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.600
While he may be a married man,

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.640
it’s not like he’s no longer a judge.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.350
Even while on his honeymoon, I’m sure that a
trivial thing like the explanation of the bread is...

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.110
<b>International Airport</b>

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.860
Let me explain to you just how wonderful this bread is.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:10.240
The fluffy dough that Azuma made using
the remix technique was improved yet further.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.450
That is, with the raw spring rolls!

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:17.960
As you know, the wrap of raw spring rolls is
made with rice paper, which is made of rice.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.250
While Azuma was making the bread,

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.920
Kanmuri wrapped the cola-brewed seaweed with rice paper,

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.420
making seaweed spring rolls!

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.680
If you were to just stuff
cola-brewed seaweed into dough,

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:35.390
the water content of the seaweed would turn
your nice and fluffy dough info a sticky mess.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.230
Therefore!

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:43.940
He wrapped it in rice paper and
then baked it inside the dough.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.410
Darling, can I please get your signature on this?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:55.160
All you think about is bread.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.120
I wanted you to look at me a little as well.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.670
It was short, but...

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.790
Thank you for everything.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:04.800
Can I just say one thing?

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.590
Seaweed goes well with rice.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.380
It also goes well with freshly baked bread.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.300
Azuma’s bread was truly wonderful!

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:17.350
And that was the video of my honeymoon.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.810
I hope that you have comprehended
just how wonderful Azuma’s bread was.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.350
A honeymoon...?

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:23.860
What about your wife, Kuro-yan?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:24.650
I divorced her.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:25.320
That was quick!

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:29.700
You managed to wrap up a honeymoon
and a divorce in that short a period?

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:30.570
And...

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:34.330
I really don’t know what to think of an explanation
about bread on your own honeymoon...

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.410
More importantly...

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.080
When exactly did Kuroyanagi-san get back?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.620
Well anyway, we know that
Azuma’s bread was wonderful.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:43.080
With this, we might be able to win.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.790
Yep.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.840
I’m done as well.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:55.350
Judge Shima... I mean Kuroyanagi...

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.430
Please sample it.

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.680
Right. Let’s have it then.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:07.230
If looks like he’s begun to
sample Miki-san’s bread, but...

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.570
I’m guessing that there can’t
be many things that can surpass

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.200
a reaction with 14 people with Shima in
their name plus a wedding to Ms. Shima.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.410
Our victory is within grasp.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.490
We can relax and watch the reaction.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:19.660
Right, Tsukino?

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:25.000
No, I really can’t relax and watch it.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:25.880
Why not?

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.670
Because your face... Kawachi-san...

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.180
Huh? My face?

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:30.630
Huh? A compact?

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.340
Wh... What was that?!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.890
O-Oh, no! Me too!

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.640
Me too!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.640
Wh-What in the world is this phenomenon?!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.640
Monet!!!

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.100
I see!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.900
This is in the style of the famous impressionist Monet!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:48.480
We’ve been trapped in Monet’s world!

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:49.730
Did you say Monet?!

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:51.990
B-But how can this be?!

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.410
What does Monet have to do with the bread he just...?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.370
W-Wait...

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.910
Momoya...

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.910
Monet-ya!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.040
Th-This is amazing!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.460
The whole grounds have turned into a Monet!

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.340
Do we have to stay like this forever?

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:09.880
No, I’m sure it’s all right.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.260
A reaction of this great a magnitude
should fizzle out soon enough.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.130
Y-You’re right!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.800
This bread is wonderful and
can be summed up in one word.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:19.850
The victor is...

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:21.850
St. Pierre!

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.100
What was that?!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.110
K-Kawachi-san’s face has now become...

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:30.360
A Sharaku painting!!

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.730
Wh... Why?!

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.570
Oh?! You mean that
Kuroyanagi’s reaction is still running?!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.820
Getting to Norihei’s bread...

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.120
The first cause of victory was the filling!

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.620
Briefly stewed seaweed that is preserved with soy!

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.080
Briefly stewed seaweed?!

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:48.870
Normally, when making preserved seaweed,
you stew it for a little more than an hour.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.840
But this seaweed has been
barely stewed for 30 minutes.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:56.630
B-But... Uppurui seaweed is strong
enough to be used as an overcoat.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.350
How can you make it soft
in just 30 minutes?

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.060
That is because...

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:03.020
It’s fresh seaweed!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.350
My hair is fresh seaweed?!

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:11.020
It’s true that you’d need more than one hour
if you try and preserve hard dried seaweed.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:15.280
But, since fresh seaweed softens easily, it
is not necessary to stew it for a long time.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.570
I-Is that so?

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.400
If you only stew it for a short time,

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:22.160
you can make it soft while preserving the flavor of the seaweed.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.910
T-To think such a strategy existed...

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:28.170
And the other cause of his victory was...

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.880
Pâte phyllo!

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.420
P-Pâte phyllo?!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.880
Don’t use my face for your explanations!

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:39.470
Pâte phyllo is an Arab sweet with a
crispy consistency made of corn and wheat.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:44.010
Norihei covered his seaweed with the
pâte phyllo and put it into his bread.

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:47.810
The bread itself did not have any
strategies except the creaming technique.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:52.860
But the combination of the pâte phyllo
with the creamed dough was truly amazing.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:55.360
N-Now I’m a sunflower?!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:19:00.360
B-But, Norihei-san’s dough had
only the creaming technique used on it.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:05.700
Azuma’s dough had two strategies: the
creaming technique and the remix technique!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.500
Then, shouldn’t Azuma’s bread be better?

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:14.420
Also, wasn’t Azuma’s bread really fluffy like rice?

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.010
Yeah, it was fluffy.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:20.430
But... that is precisely the biggest reason for your loss!

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:21.930
What was that?!

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:24.680
It’s true that your bread was fluffy.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.470
It went well with the seaweed too.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.430
But...

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:28.890
No matter how fluffy you try to make it,

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.980
bread is bread, and rice is rice.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:35.690
No matter how close a bread tries to get
to rice, it can’t stand up to the real thing.

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:36.820
And...

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:41.200
I feel that the seaweed should have been
brewed for about 30 minutes less in the cola.

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.450
Also, if you’re to make it
go well with bread,

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.040
rather than using something hard to chew like rice paper,

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:50.210
it’s better to use something crispy like pâte phyllo.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.750
No doubt that Azuma’s bread was wonderful.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:54.460
But...

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.670
Norihei’s bread went over and beyond that.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.920
It can be called a truly artistic bread!

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.680
And art is... explosive!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.190
Please, don’t look so down.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.770
Please cheer up.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.780
The guy from Momoya...

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.950
In matches like these over a specialty product,

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.490
there are weaknesses and strengths
to preparing that specialty product.

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:28.200
It can’t be helped that you lost.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:32.830
This time, the specialty
product was advantageous to me.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:37.300
It is obvious that if you just look at
the dough, your strategy was way better.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.090
You needn’t feel ashamed.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:41.880
Oh, that’s right.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.510
I wanted to give this to you.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.010
Norihei’s seaweed recipes

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:48.350
What is this?

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:54.100
These are recipes using seaweed that I’ve worked
on day and night over the years to come up with.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:21:00.230
Well, I don’t think seaweed will come up as
a specialty product in a main match anymore,

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:05.240
but seaweed is not limited to Uppurui
and can be harvested all over Japan.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:08.300
So, I’m sure that you may be able to use seaweed

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:12.000
as an accent to turn the match
in your favor.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.500
Th-That’s true, but...

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.750
Why are you helping me so much?

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:21.250
That’s because I was moved
by your goal of making <i>Japan</i>.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:27.390
The influx of cuisines from all over the
world is something that cannot be helped.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:33.270
But, if we just accept them without thought,
then our indigenous cuisine will be lost.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:40.360
You’re trying to reinvent a Western food item
like bread at the hands of a Japanese person.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:42.190
Such artisans are necessary for the Japan of the future.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:44.740
We are also further researching how

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.700
we can continue to make things like preserved seaweed

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:51.200
go better with Japan’s characteristic foods.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.460
So, let’s both do our best.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:07.090
He was a really nice person.

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:07.890
Yeah.

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.930
As far as the results go, we lost...

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.850
but I think we’ve still gained a lot more.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:13.560
Yeah.

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:17.060
Let’s pull ourselves together and try once again.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:17.980
Yep!

00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:20.230
That’s the way, guys.

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:22.320
I’m looking forward to the next match.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:27.030
Umm... It looks like everyone has reached an ending that makes them happy, but...

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:32.580
There’s no follow-up to the fact that my face
has been messed up like a Picasso painting...

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:44.090
Robbie, come on out to the sound of the voice calling you.

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:52.010
Robbie, you were crying all by yourself.

00:22:52.180 --> 00:23:00.350
Robbie, the eyes in your heart...

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:03.820
what is it that they reflect?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:07.240
...Is it “Who am I?”...

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:15.030
The other side of the mirage flickers faintly.

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:23.630
Anywhere is fine, as long as it’s not here.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:32.340
My dancing heart is reborn as a marble time and again.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:36.470
The colors I just filled in were yours.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:40.390
It’s not something that will finish with a turn. Be load.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:48.320
Just like your joy, try letting your tears flow.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:52.410
See? The world is filled in with your colors.

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:59.080
Like a tumble, do the best of you.

00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:06.850
He’s coming...

00:24:06.850 --> 00:24:08.100
He’s sure to come...

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.850
He’s... He’s back after one year!

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:11.690
A panda?!

00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:13.850
Could it be that the panda’s identity is...?

00:24:13.860 --> 00:24:15.190
No!!!

00:24:15.190 --> 00:24:16.400
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.400 --> 00:24:17.850
A fearful revenge!!

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.140
The panda man appears!

00:24:19.140 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.250 --> 00:24:26.040
Impressionism is best represented
by the French painter, Claude Monet.

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:26.670
Monet pursued new forms of lighting and coloring

00:24:26.670 --> 00:24:27.370
Pursued new forms of lighting and coloring

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:29.210
to capture the changing era and the seasons...

00:24:29.210 --> 00:24:29.470
He was also known as the Painter of Light.

00:24:29.470 --> 00:24:31.750
Painter of Light
He was also known as the Painter of Light.

00:24:32.300 --> 00:24:34.470
Oh?!
